From: Arctic Linux maintainers
Subject: [PATCH] Complete forced-software frames before releasing the render buffer

Arctic's Safe graphics session and greeter select SceneFX's existing
WLR_RENDERER_FORCE_SOFTWARE=1 EGL path. In the non-timeline submit branch,
complete that frame while its EGL context and render buffer are still held.
An owned same-image default/completion trial removed the observed stale
scanout regions; initial boot and installed-image validation remain required.

Keep the normal hardware and explicit signal-timeline paths unchanged. Check
the existing exact boolean without env_parse_bool's per-frame logging.

--- a/render/fx_renderer/fx_pass.c
+++ b/render/fx_renderer/fx_pass.c
@@ -3,6 +3,7 @@
 #include <stdlib.h>
 #include <assert.h>
 #include <pixman.h>
+#include <string.h>
 #include <time.h>
 #include <unistd.h>
 #include <wlr/render/allocator.h>
@@ -147,6 +148,12 @@
 		}
 	} else {
 		glFlush();
+		// Safe graphics explicitly selects software EGL with this option.
+		// Complete writes before restoring the context and unlocking the buffer.
+		const char *force_software = getenv("WLR_RENDERER_FORCE_SOFTWARE");
+		if (force_software != NULL && strcmp(force_software, "1") == 0) {
+			glFinish();
+		}
 	}
 
 	ok = true;
